  "view_recipe": "Complete original1..4 views, then side=min(width,height,640) squares, stride=floor(3*side/4), evenly distributed integer offsets and y-major order; deduplicate with original prefix. Reject inventories over16. For1280x720: original4 plus six640px crops =10.",
  "evaluation": "New inference on viewed original8 and fresh16: first and repeated optimized S Resize2x plans, then serial original S ONNX plan on all10 views. 24*10*3=720 forwards; no warmup. Score unchanged coarse4, naive10 and supported10 from the same measured views. This is an offline capacity/augmentation comparison, without a new timing or availability claim. Also run the frozen Nano four-view optimized detector twice on the same24 images (192 forwards) to separate model capacity from supplementation; total912 new forwards. Nano receives the unchanged original four views, not the640px supplemental grid.",
  "relative_adoption": "In each group supported precision must not regress against coarse and must exceed naive, recall must exceed coarse without per-present-class recall regression. Fresh16 must also pass all original absolute quality gates. No adoption on partial success.",
  "model_choice": "Reuse the independently pinned cached official YOLOX-S640 model and existing guarded Resize2x lowering. Fixed before new inputs; no training, score sweep, class-specific threshold or changed support rule.",
  "capacity_comparison": "Report S coarse4 versus Nano coarse4 on the same fixed groups, independently from S supported versus S coarse. Fixed thresholds and complete mapped original labels; no capacity gain claim by comparisons on different images."
}
